---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
const scholar = 'https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ngAHmhEAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao';
---
<Base title="Research">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Research</h1>
    <div class="grid"><p class="span-8">Applied HCI in the places technology was not designed for.</p></div>
  </header>

  <Section label="Statement" title="What I study">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p>Technology is designed in large, stable rooms and used in small, moving, improvised ones. My research follows it there: vans lived in full time, schools with one counsellor for two thousand students, families reading a wellbeing report at a kitchen table, a card game played across two countries. I ask what the design assumed, what the setting does to that assumption, and what a system built for the setting would look like. The answer is usually an artefact, so I build it and put it back in the field.</p>
      <p>Current threads: stigma-aware communication of child wellbeing in Indian schools; programmable physical objects for play; and methods work on how access to field sites compounds across studies.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Doctorate" title="Thesis">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p><em>Towards Design of Interaction Systems for Constrained Spaces.</em> University of Waterloo, 2025. Supervised by Mark Hancock.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Publications">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p><a href={scholar} target="_blank" rel="noopener">All papers on Google Scholar</a>, including CHI, Graphics Interface, CHI PLAY, and Interactive Health, with two under review.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Teaching">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p>Nine courses at Waterloo between 2021 and 2024, undergraduate and graduate, in classes of 40 to 180: Introduction to UX, Advanced UX Design and Research, the UX research seminar, the undergraduate capstone, Human-Computer Interaction, and Analytics and User Experience. Around 700 students from nine departments.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Service">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p>Reviewer for CHI, CSCW, and CUI with outstanding-reviewer recognition at each; Local Arrangements Chair, CHI PLAY 2023; programme committee for a CSCW 2024 workshop on evaluating UX outcomes at scale.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p class="label">Documents</p>
      <p><a href="/cv.pdf">Academic CV (PDF)</a></p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
</Base>
